Subject: [PATCH] Detect D3D11 loss before frames and guard failed resources

Query native removal before onscreen and offscreen frames, classify resource
failures without treating ordinary allocation errors as device loss, and keep
failed dynamic buffers and native resources out of upload/copy operations.
Complete failed readbacks and release their update batches.

Based on Qt 6.11.2 with upstream backports 0064 through 0066.

diff --git a/src/gui/rhi/qrhid3d11.cpp b/src/gui/rhi/qrhid3d11.cpp
index cb2d12f..e42f011 100644
--- a/src/gui/rhi/qrhid3d11.cpp
+++ b/src/gui/rhi/qrhid3d11.cpp
@@ -791,6 +791,19 @@ bool QRhiD3D11::isDeviceLost() const
     return deviceLost;
 }
 
+bool QRhiD3D11::checkDeviceLost(HRESULT result)
+{
+    if (!deviceLost) {
+        const auto reason = dev ? dev->GetDeviceRemovedReason() : S_OK;
+        deviceLost = FAILED(reason)
+                || result == DXGI_ERROR_DEVICE_REMOVED
+                || result == DXGI_ERROR_DEVICE_RESET;
+        if (deviceLost)
+            qWarning("D3D11 device lost: %s", qPrintable(QSystemError::windowsComString(FAILED(reason) ? reason : result)));
+    }
+    return deviceLost;
+}
